MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB hub fits how I use my electronics: connecting my card reader and other USB accessories without repeatedly swapping connections would solve a practical problem.",
    "The Fire HD 8 feels like a natural upgrade from my Fire 7 because a larger screen and more storage would improve portable viewing. A Fire TV stick also fits my television use by adding convenient streaming, even though my 720p television would not benefit from 4K."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "My photography purchases do not imply a need for home surveillance, and my memory-card purchases do not mean I have an internal SSD to put in an enclosure. Those products serve different tasks from the ones my accessories support.",
    "The gaming controller, voice assistant, and earbuds do not address a current need for me. Buying a cable for an older Apple device also does not establish that AirPods would fit my everyday setup."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning a Fire tablet seems to have been taken as interest in a wider range of Amazon devices, although gaming and voice assistance are not what I am looking for.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in gadgets, when my choices usually have a specific purpose involving connections, storage, photography, or viewing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of adapters, cables, card accessories, and mounts suggest that making devices work together matters to me. The USB hub follows that pattern particularly well.",
    "Compatibility and an actual improvement matter: a larger tablet could improve my viewing, but 4K adds little on my current television, and I would only need one of the similar streaming sticks."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in practical accessories and viewing, but stretched that interest into devices for needs I have not shown."
}
